SOC=all (one kernel for SM8550 and SM8650, see build.sh)

rocknix/  ROCKNIX device patches rebased for the combined tree. A file here
          replaces ROCKNIX's patch of the same name. For the other SoC's
          patches (context only where they touched the same lines):
  0063-gpu-drm-panel-add-pocket-fit-panel.patch (SM8650): Makefile hunk
          after the SM8550 AR06/AR02 panel lines.
          For Linux 7.3 + ../retroid (ROCKNIX's recipe is for 7.2):
  0001-pcie-update-sm8550-dtsi.patch (SM8550): context only (7.3 labels
          the root ports pcie0_port0/pcie1_port0).
  0007-audioreach-Add-dedicated-WSA2-support.patch (SM8650): 7.3 builds
          the active channel mask from the channel map; that is the else
          branch now.
  0036_ASoC--qcom--sc8280xp-Add-support-for-Primary-I2S.patch (SM8550):
          7.3 has per-card MI2S data (priv, hw_params); keeps it and adds
          the optional i2s_clk and the Primary MI2S startup/shutdown.
  0051, 0056 (SM8550 panels): Kconfig/Makefile context only.
  0053-gpu-panel-st7703-add-Pocket-DS-lower-panel.patch (SM8550): 7.3
          has the Pocket DS lower panel; only the optional avee rail is
          left.
  0057_Chipone-ICNA35XX-panel.patch (SM8550): 7.3 has a different
          panel-chipone-icna35xx.c (per-device ayntec,* compatibles). Ours
          replaces it whole: the AYN DTS use chipone,icna3512/3520 and
          ../sm8550/patches/0651/0652 are written against it. Kconfig and
          Makefile already have the entry.
  0057_DDIC-CH13726A-panel.patch (SM8550): Kconfig context (7.3's own
          panel-chipwealth-ch13726a.c matches ayntec,thor-panel-bottom,
          ours ch13726a,* - no clash).
  0060-Add-Silergy-SY7758-backlight-driver.patch (SM8650): 7.3 has an
          upstream sy7758.c; ROCKNIX's replaces it whole (the one the
          Pocket FIT and Pocket S2 were tested with). Kconfig and Makefile
          already have the entry.

patches/  port patches for the combined tree only, queued with the port
          patches by name:
  0506-mailbox-qcom-ipcc-every-soc-counts-its-doorbell-wakes.patch: on top
          of SM8550 0504/0505, gives SM8650 the "ipcc-wake" count (SM8650's
          0019 is written against the unmasked driver).

port-skip SM8650 port patches the combined tree leaves out (each replaced by
          an SM8550 twin or a patch in patches/). Port patches whose code is
          identical to the other SoC's (e.g. SM8650 0021 = SM8550 0539) are
          dropped automatically.
